# Runtime Loop-Native Audit Verdict

Verdict: `runtime_loop_native_product_answer_lanes_proven`

This pass targeted the same disease we identified in the web and artifact lanes: deterministic answer-shaping trying to stand in for iterative model cognition. The product boundary is now cleaner in the audited paths:

- Web answer lanes keep retrieved evidence as typed context and require model-authored finalization.
- Delegation prep fallback no longer authors prose; it records typed prep status for the child run.
- Static website artifacts no longer fabricate canned HTML/CSS/JS when the selected model fails to provide source.
- Fixture/local:auto model records remain hidden or rejected from product defaults unless fixture mode is explicitly enabled.
- Story/run-date/confidence markers remain only as detectors, parsers, tests, or trace-only metadata, not product answer copy.

## Fixes

1. `crates/services/src/agentic/runtime/service/lifecycle/delegation/prep.rs`
   - Replaced fallback prep prose with typed context:
     `prep_mode`, `memory_retrieval_status`, and `next_context_source`.

2. `packages/runtime-daemon/src/conversation-artifacts.mjs`
   - Removed the canned static website generator.
   - Static website artifact create/edit/rebuild/compare now require model-authored HTML/CSS/JS.
   - Removed deterministic wording from generic export paths.

3. `packages/runtime-daemon/src/conversation-artifacts.test.mjs`
   - Updated coverage so source-less static website creation fails closed.
   - Preserved model-authored HTML/CSS/JS render coverage.

